---
/*
Two-tone page split (Lucide-style): the tone change alone marks the sidebar
boundary, with no divider line. Render it once inside any page that uses the
shared two-column shell (18rem sidebar + gap-10 inside Base's max-w-7xl px-4
main), and pass `split` to Base so the Header/Footer bands carry the same
boundary through the chrome.

How the tones are layered — the CARD side comes from the canvas, not this
component: on split pages html:has(...) (theme.css) paints the canvas bg-card
(the canvas owns the page background; body stays background-free so -z-10
layers like this one show through). This layer paints the OTHER side:
bg-background from the viewport's left edge to the boundary.

How the geometry works:
- The layer is absolute inside Base's `relative min-h-screen` wrapper, so
  inset-y-0 spans the full page height (the 100dvh tool page and normally
  scrolling pages alike) and % offsets resolve against the same width the
  centered container uses.
- right comes from the shared `split-sidebar-boundary` utility (theme.css),
  fed by --split-boundary-x, which puts the tone change mid-gap. Keep that
  property in sync with the shell geometry.
- left = calc(50% - 50vw) bleeds to the true viewport edge.
- -z-10 paints under all content but above the canvas background (html owns
  the page background; theme.css base layer), which is why neither body nor
  Base's wrapper may carry a background of their own.
Below md the boundary resolves to 0, so this layer collapses to nothing and
the card canvas spans the full width — the content keeps the same surface
color it has in the desktop content column.
*/
---

<div
  aria-hidden="true"
  class="split-sidebar-boundary pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 left-[calc(50%_-_50vw)] -z-10 bg-background"
>
</div>
